# device-layer-0009.
# The battery: how full it is and whether it is charging, through UIDevice on iOS, the power sources on macOS
# (IOKit), BatteryManager on Android and navigator.getBattery in a browser.
#
#   battery-status   `<level> <state>`: the level from 0 to 1 to two places (or `unknown`), and charging, full,
#                    unplugged or unknown. `unavailable` with no battery (a desktop, the simulator)
#
# A host with no such capability (the server, the memory host) answers `unavailable`. Every answer is text from the
# closed set above, so an app compares strings and no platform enum ever reaches it.

load ./native/{platform}/battery
  find read-battery
  find follow-battery

task battery-status
  like text
  send back
    call read-battery

# the answer above now and at every change the platform reports, to `handler`, until the task it answers is called.
# Any number at once, each dropped by its own task, and one subscription to the platform between them, ended by
# the last drop. A watcher started while others run hears the current answer at once
task watch-battery
  take handler
    like task
      take value, like text
  like task
  send back
    call follow-battery
      read handler
